> **In one sentence:** confirm five things with the owner of the Verisk agreement before building.

| # | Question to confirm | Needed for | If the answer is no |
|:-:|---|---|---|
| 1 | Are hypothetical "what-if" calls permitted, and how are they priced? | Option B, and the Option A study | Option A with engineering sensitivities |
| 2 | May we store relative effects (log-ratios) derived from a designed batch of calls? | Option A | Engineering or published cost-guide sensitivities |
| 3 | May we aggregate stored MERCs across properties into neighborhood \$/sqft references? | Neighborhood check | External regional \$/sqft benchmarks |
| 4 | May realized MERC differences be used to **evaluate** (not train) the score? | Validation | Validate at the attribute level only |
| 5 | What does per-call pricing mean for each option? | Everything | — |

> ⚖️ **Design principle:** nothing here fits a model with MERC as the outcome. MERC is only ever *looked up* (final and what-if calls) or *compared* (the neighborhood check and validation). Whether that satisfies the agreement is for its owner to confirm.

