## Appendix A: Notation cheat sheet

| Symbol | Plain English | Comes from |
|:-:|---|---|
| $p_k$ | Confidence that attribute $k$'s prefill value is correct | Attribute model (step 3) |
| $W_k$ | 1 if attribute $k$ is actually wrong, 0 if not | Simulated: 1 with probability $1 - p_k$ |
| $\Delta_k$ | Change in log-MERC if attribute $k$ took its corrected value | Option A table or Option B call |
| $e_k$ | Elasticity: % change in MERC per % change in a continuous attribute | Option A table or Option B call |
| $D$ | Leftover attribute error | Simulation |
| $\varepsilon_V$ | Engine error | Verisk |
| $\sigma_V$ | Spread of the engine error | Verisk's range |
| $E$ | Total error, $D + \varepsilon_V$ | Both of the above |
| $\tau_{\text{under}}, \tau_{\text{over}}$ | How far too low or too high the MERC may be | Business decision |
| $C$ | MERC confidence: the chance $E$ is within tolerance | This method |
| $m_k$ | Materiality: chance wrong × typical impact | Option B screening |
| $w, k$ | Blending weight, and the cell size that earns half the weight | H3 neighborhood reference |
| $z$ | Neighborhood \$/sqft score | H3 neighborhood reference |

